0 !THEME Architecture
0 !KEYWORDS France, building, monument, cathedral, church, medieval
0 !KEYWORDS choir, nave, transept, clerestory, rose window
0 !KEYWORDS tower, bells, spire, flèche, rib vault, flying buttress
0 !KEYWORDS Jean de Chelles, Pierre de Montreuil, gothic, Rayonnant
0 !KEYWORDS Jean-Baptiste Lassus, Eugène Viollet-le-Duc

0 // Release year: 2024
0 // No. of pieces: 4383
0 // Collection: Landmarks
0 // Designer: Rok Žgalin Kobe

0 // The official part count includes a brick separator
0 // and an unused candle element (no. 37762).

0 // Set 21061 was released in June 2024, ahead of the Olympic Games held in
0 // Paris that summer and in anticipation of the cathedral's planned reopening
0 // following the 2019 fire that destroyed the roof and spire. The construction
0 // timeline of the real cathedral is reflected in the model's innovative build
0 // process, which is arranged into five historical stages spanning the years
0 // 1163 through 1860. The model, which includes a removable roof section, is
0 // further divided into 34 numbered building phases.

0 // ~~ Building statistics ~~
0 // Location: Paris, France
0 // Commissioned by: Maurice de Sully
0 // Constructed: 1163–1345
0 // Major restorations: 1844–1864, 2020–
0 // Materials: Limestone, wood, lead
0 // Height: 226 ft / 68.9 m
0 // Spire height: 315 ft / 96.0 m
0 // No. of floors: 3

0 // ~ [ 1163–1182 ] ~
0 // The choir, or chancel, comprising the rounded eastern end
0 // of the cathedral, is the first section to be constructed.

0 // ~ Phase 1 ~

